# Fixed (lib/sake/typer_eval.rb): a branch that a narrowing leaves no value for is not run (it was run, only its
# result left out, since 56ba59b6); also the right of `x && f(x)` and a loop body. This prints 2 and
# controller_conditional_get passes. Sample: test/samples/void_branch_not_run.strict.sake.
# A call in a branch that a nil-only value never takes still gives a type: in headers() last_modified is only nil,
# so `if last_modified` narrows it to nothing, but Time.httpdate runs on the empty value, its `case x in Time ...
# in String then Core.parse_httpdate(x)` runs the String branch anyway (parse_httpdate makes a Time from the regexp's
# captures), and the Time lands in the Hash: "String.size: argument 1 must be String, but can be Time".
# Ruby: the branch is not run; this prints 2. Not caused by 04cea37b (the same with fbfd2733).
# Seen in test/sakelib/rails/actionpack/controller_conditional_get.sake once the checker got past the construction:
# ActionController::ConditionalGet#fresh_when's `response.last_modified = last_modified if last_modified` with no
# last_modified put a Time among the response headers, and ActionDispatch::SSL's flag_cookies_as_secure! read it as
# a set-cookie value (ssl.sake:65, 67). No natural workaround: the test is left failing.
require "time"
def headers(last_modified = nil)
  h = Hash.new
  h["etag"] = "v1"
  h["last-modified"] = Time.httpdate(last_modified) if last_modified
  h
end
v = headers()["etag"]
p(String.size(v)) if v
